@startuml usecases-access
' page: landscape
!include _usecase-style.puml
title Access use cases (draft)

' Shows who starts which Access use case, and where Keycloak takes part.
' Not drawn: the rules each use case applies, and the other contexts (Projects, Evaluations).
' Evolved from MK3 UC-A1 to UC-A7. MK3 UC-A7 is UC-A2 here (see the source specs).
' Green = built. Grey = not built (UC-A15 is Release 2).


actor "Person\n(not signed in)" as Visitor #1565C0
actor "Signed-in\nperson" as Member #1565C0
actor "Administrator" as Admin #E65100
actor "Keycloak" as KC #6B7280

rectangle "Access (BC-ACCESS)" #F2F6FC {
  usecase "UC-A10\nSign in" as UCA10 COLOR_BUILT
  usecase "UC-A12\nRegister and wait\nfor approval" as UCA12 COLOR_BUILT
  usecase "UC-A15\nSign in through\ncompany SSO" as UCA15 COLOR_TODO
  usecase "UC-A11\nSign out" as UCA11 COLOR_BUILT
  usecase "UC-A13\nView my name\nand role" as UCA13 COLOR_BUILT
  usecase "UC-A14\nKeep the session\nalive" as UCA14 COLOR_BUILT
  usecase "UC-A2\nApprove, deactivate\nand reinstate an account" as UCA2 COLOR_BUILT
}

UCA10 -[hidden]right-> UCA12
UCA12 -[hidden]right-> UCA15
UCA11 -[hidden]right-> UCA13
UCA13 -[hidden]right-> UCA14
UCA10 -[hidden]down-> UCA11
UCA14 -[hidden]right-> UCA2
Visitor --> UCA10
Visitor --> UCA12
Visitor --> UCA15
Member --> UCA11
Member --> UCA13
Admin --> UCA2

' UC-A14 is started by the web server on the person's behalf, so it is drawn as included.
UCA13 .> UCA14 : <<include>>
UCA2 .> UCA14 : <<include>>

' Keycloak takes part in these (it holds the login, the session and the enabled flag).
UCA10 -- KC
UCA12 -- KC
UCA15 -- KC
UCA11 -- KC
UCA14 -- KC
UCA2 -- KC

legend bottom right
  Green: built. Grey: not built.
  Keycloak is a secondary actor: it proves who the person is.
  Playground's account decides what the person may do.
endlegend
@enduml
